a. The text-related pieces are side inputs rather than a substantive text-bio model bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"initialises every node with a frozen foundation-model representation (scVI, ESM-2 and ChemBERTa)\"; \"learns a tissue’s communication network directly from spatial transcriptomics\""},{"record_id":"rec_000112","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this paper is a review summarizing AI-driven multi-omics approaches for breast cancer. It is not a primary candidate model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review aims to summarize recent developments\"; \"We have also highlighted the integration of omics-based data\""}]}
